  "scientific_status": "Exact full-Fock adjacent-charge transfer is represented by the body-loss operator D. Weighted compact-time replacement by the whole-field G source and summable ordinary-power/force tails are established in the manuscript. Nilpotent source normalization retains internal Gaussian contractions and identifies the charge-static background already present in G2. Full joint charge-energy regression and charged AA/AB/BA spectra remain open.",
  "parameters": "Standard CAR, overlapping complex Gaussian p-body model, same original J across charges, annealed normalized beta=mu=0 full trace, hbar=1/string time; even N, p to infinity, lambda_N=p^2/N tending to positive lambda, fixed Js. Memory times are in fixed compact intervals; polynomial degrees are fixed before the double-scale limit. Finite integer checks use a separate 2/1 variance.",
  "proof_scope": "Saved finite identities, selected CAR words, signed local graph coefficients and full-binomial numerical sums check the recorded assertions at their specified parameters. They do not by themselves prove weighted all-time bounds, arbitrary-degree Poisson geometry or a static-subtraction theorem. Those manuscript arguments and the unresolved joint charge-energy regression are distinguished explicitly. No-Gaussian-bridge does not remove charge-static correlations in whole-field oriented sources.",
  "continuation": "Construct the joint charge-energy regression of G_n and K_n, recover the known low-order A0 and nonzero A0/B2 mixed calibration after proper static subtraction, and determine AA/AB/BA. Then combine with the neutral kernel before returning to the Susskind bulk dictionary and interactions.",
